# migrated from tests/cases/induce.chat (gen346, hermetic + isolated)
[mock hermetic]
!set PARROT0_BASE=
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test induce]
# Generation 7: induction — learn rules from the facts (the "training").
> socrates is a man
< Learned: socrates is a man.
> socrates is a mortal
< Learned: socrates is a mortal.
> plato is a man
< Learned: plato is a man.
> plato is a mortal
< Learned: plato is a mortal.
# A counterexample for the reverse direction: a mortal who is not a man.
> rex is a dog
< Learned: rex is a dog.
> rex is a mortal
< Learned: rex is a mortal.
# Induce: every man is mortal (2+ examples, no counterexample); NOT the
# reverse (rex is mortal but not a man), and NOT dog->mortal (only 1 example).
> generalize
< Induced: mortal(X) :- man(X).
# The induced rule generalizes to a brand-new individual never seen as mortal.
> aristotle is a man
< Learned: aristotle is a man.
> is aristotle a mortal?
< Yes.
# Nothing left to learn from the current facts.
> generalize
< Nothing new to generalize.

